<title>POLAND: Polish wheat, rye prices up last week, barley down.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat, rye prices up last week, barley down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish average wheat and rye prices rose while barley eased at grain auctions in the week ending on August 11, the Agriculture Ministry said in a</p>
<p>statement on Monday.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>Grain  Week to Aug 11 previous week month/month  yr/yr change</p>
<p>Wheat    57.31 zl/q    56.55 zl/q	3.9 pct     -9.0 pct</p>
<p>Rye	42.40 zl/q    42.07 zl/q	6.0 pct	6.6 pct</p>
<p>Barley   49.23 zl/q    50.02 zl/q	3.2 pct     -9.3 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
